==Battleground==
*2 [[Axoloty|Axoloties]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[LeMurr]] spawns after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*3 [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*2 [[LeMurr]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is fairly easy on 1-crown and 4-crown. Players should lure and eliminate the first LeMurr, then deploy Talented [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to nuke Axoloty. Bring other rushers as well as [[Cadaver BearCat]] for the Zombies and victory is practically guaranteed.

On higher crown difficulties, however, caution is advised, since as with many earlier UL Subchapters a large multiplier is applied to the already high enemy strength magnifications on 2-3 crown, forcing the deployment of specialist units or even Ubers. Thankfully, the Zackie Pengs have single target with a very long respawn delay, while the other threats will eventually dry up, leaving players with a mostly clear shot at the Axoloties.

===3 Crown Strategy===
This stage is not very free. Thanks to  UL's magnifications, every enemy here genuinely becomes a threat, including Axoloty, who now has 720,000 damage and will kill everyone if he gets the chance to attack. Thankfully, [[Royal Guard Cat]] exists. Use [[Soap Cat]], Seafarer, and Guard to chip the first Axoloty, then try to get as much damage onto the Axoloty as you can. The Zombies are no joke either, so run [[Shigong Cat]], BearCat, and [[Cat Chief]] for them.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] - A great anti-Alien CC unit, Seafarer has 100% chance to Survive a Lethal Strike and 40% chance to Freeze Aliens for 4 seconds. This is mostly useful against LeMurr when paired with meatshields, but also helps for rushing down Axoloty by exploiting its long foreswing.
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard]] - Royal Guard is one of the few 4-crown Wave Immune options available here, having a relatively low cost and Massive Damage against Aliens. It can simply dismiss Axoloty's Wave, and, if protected properly, will melt through LeMurr's HP, being also useful for chipping Axoloty during cleanup.
*[[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong]] - With how dangerous the Zombies can get, an anti-Zombie specialist meatshield with resistance to them is absolutely necessary to pin them.

===Recommended Ubers===
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Thanks to his unusually low cooldown/cost for an Uber and his very high stats, he can inflict serious damage and quickly take out whatever that gets in the way, especially after his talents are factored in, as his Single Attack isn't of much concern. While he can't be expected to survive for long, Greater Balrog nonetheless will see multiple deployments.

==Trivia==
*A dead zone is an area of the ocean in which oxygen levels are too low to support most marine life, frequently due to eutrophication (excessive richness of nutrients in a body of water) and pollution.
*Endless Dead Zone's Japanese name, Shikai Naki Shikai (視界なき死海, "Dead Sea Without Visibility"), plays off of how 視界 (visibility) sounds the same as 死海 (dead sea).

